      "id": "cm02-forces-initial-data-and-newtonian-flow-examples",
      "location": "Paragraph beginning “The counterexamples probe the hypotheses.”",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The page gives the nonuniqueness force as “$F(x)=m\\sqrt{|x_{1}|}\\,e_{1}$” for a unit-mass model. Under `def-cm01-units`, mass has dimension $\\mu$ and position has dimension $\\ell$, so this expression has dimension $\\mu\\ell^{1/2}$, not force dimension $\\mu\\ell\\tau^{-2}$. The current counterexample item instead uses $\\lambda\\sqrt{|x_1|/\\ell_*}$ and declares the dimensions of $\\lambda$ and $\\ell_*$.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "dd92f6a4298d24928713bf74bfd180a21f5c7d9814dd4c0e40e9b61691044ac2"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:18:2",
      "id": "ex-cm02-uniform-field",
      "location": "Example, claim 2",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The setup specifies $N$ labels, $Q=\\mathbb R^{3N}$, and $\\mathbf g\\in\\mathbb R^3$, then claims the model motion is $x(t)=x_0+v_0t+\\tfrac12\\mathbf g t^2$. `def-cm02-newtonian-flow` defines a motion as $x:J\\to Q$ and initial data with $x_0\\in Q$, $v_0\\in(\\mathbb R^3)^N$. Thus for $N>1$ the displayed sum is not typed: a single 3-vector cannot be added to the full configuration. The item does not set $N=1$ here or define the repeated tuple of field vectors.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "ea62d06cb500703d98569e82bc09b790f47c9ba4740f8f80d86d2cc1d0d1b82d"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:18:3",
      "id": "pthm-cm02-continuation",
      "location": "Title",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The title claims “finite-time breakdown requires escape from every compact subset of the state domain.” But Statement clause 2 concerns compact subsets of $D=I_0\\times U$, while clause 4 requires $I_0=\\mathbb R$ before concluding state escape. For a counterexample, take $I_0=(0,1)$, $Q=\\mathbb R^{3N}$, $F\\equiv0$, and zero initial velocity. The constant state has maximal interval $(0,1)$ and remains in a compact singleton of $U$ as its finite right endpoint is reached. Only the time-state graph leaves compact subsets of $D$.",
